{
  "title": { "en": "Two islanders" },
  "intro": [{ "t": { "en": "b says nothing, but what a says mentions him." } }],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "kk-two_1",
      "kind": "gates",
      "tray": "gates",
      "step": { "en": "Translate" },
      "blind": true,
      "target": "KA ↔ ¬KA ∧ ¬KB",
      "brief": {
        "en": "Two islanders, a and b; a says: “We are both knaves.” Wire it as a circuit: it outputs true on the rows where what a says fits what a is."
      },
      "hint": [
        { "en": "“We are both knaves” is “¬a is a knight ∧ ¬b is a knight”." }
      ],
      "solution": ["na = gNot(KA)", "nb = gNot(KB)", "both = gAnd(na, nb)", "e = gIff(KA, both)", "out <- e"]
    },
    {
      "id": "kk-two_2",
      "kind": "proof",
      "tray": "proof",
      "step": { "en": "Proof" },
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "p": "A ↔ ¬A ∧ ¬B" }, "goal": "¬A ∧ B" }],
      "cases": [{ "A": "KA", "B": "KB" }, { "A": "KC", "B": "KD" }],
      "hint": [
        {
          "en": "First prove “¬a is a knight”: suppose a is a knight, and look at what he says."
        },
        {
          "en": "If a is a knave, his statement is false. For the half about b, try proof by contradiction."
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "na = impI[A=A](body: m2) {",
        "  body {",
        "    m1 = mp(e.left, na.body)",
        "    s = andE(m1)",
        "    m2 = mp(s.left, na.body)",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "nnb = impI[A=\"~B\"](body: m3) {",
        "  body {",
        "    c = andI(na, nnb.body)",
        "    m3 = mp(t, c)",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "e = andE(p)",
        "b = raa(nnb)",
        "t = chain(e.right, na)",
        "both = andI(na, b)",
        "goal <- both"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
